From: TB520FU port maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: fix first-enable UEFI handoff stall on bonded DSI

Two defects in the first-enable path can stall the bus when the UEFI
framebuffer is still scanning (TB520FU shows the firmware image until
Gamescope first atomic commit on DSI-1, with DSI-1 enabled=disabled):

1. dsi_link_clk_set_rate_6g_v2_9() logs clk_set_parent failures and then
overwrites ret and proceeds to set rates on the wrong parent. If the
RCG reparent stalls (RCG busy from firmware scanout, parent PLL not yet
locked), the driver programs byte/pixel rates on the stale parent and
the next dsi_write in dsi_timing_setup/dsi_sw_reset stalls the AXI bus
(all CPUs freeze, no oops). Return the error so power_on aborts before
touching the hung clock.

2. msm_dsi_host_power_on() switches the byte/pixel RCGs before quiescing a
firmware-enabled controller. The MDSS reset at probe does not stop the
display when the Lucid Ole PLLs are preserved (0828), so CTRL is still
ENABLED on the first power_on (power_on==false but hardware on).
Switching RCG parents/rates underneath a streaming controller wedges the
RCG/PLL. Quiesce a firmware-enabled controller while still on the old
clocks before reparenting, mirroring the disable in dsi_sw_reset but
before the clock switch.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c	2026-10-14 12:52:53.827978514 +0900
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c	2026-10-14 18:33:33.105124616 +0900
@@ -446,12 +446,16 @@
 	 * cannot use assigned-clock-parents.
 	 */
 	ret = clk_set_parent(msm_host->byte_src_clk, msm_host->dsi_pll_byte_clk);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "Failed to parent byte_src -> dsi_pll_byte: %d\n", ret);
+		return ret;
+	}
 
 	ret = clk_set_parent(msm_host->pixel_src_clk, msm_host->dsi_pll_pixel_clk);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "Failed to parent pixel_src -> dsi_pll_pixel: %d\n", ret);
+		return ret;
+	}
 
 	return dsi_link_clk_set_rate_6g(msm_host);
 }
@@ -2549,6 +2553,18 @@
 	}
 
 	pm_runtime_get_sync(&msm_host->pdev->dev);
+
+	/*
+	 * UEFI may leave the controller streaming (firmware framebuffer still
+	 * visible, MDSS reset preserved by 0828). Switching RCGs underneath a
+	 * running controller wedges the clock and stalls the bus on the next
+	 * register access. Quiesce it on the old clocks before reparenting.
+	 */
+	if (dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_CTRL) & DSI_CTRL_ENABLE) {
+		dsi_write(msm_host, REG_DSI_CTRL, 0);
+		wmb();
+	}
+
 	ret = cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_set_rate(msm_host);
 	if (!ret)
 		ret = cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_enable(msm_host);

